   "id": "p10-long-mixed",
   "kind": "long",
   "text": "The river ran high that spring, and the town council met every evening to argue about the levee. Some wanted to raise it by a metre; others said the money would be better spent moving the houses on the low road further up the hill. Nobody could agree on who should pay, and in the end the water decided for them: on the first warm night in April it came over the top near the old mill, quietly, and by morning the low road was a canal. The children loved it. Their parents did not.\n\ndef merge_sorted(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Merge two sorted lists into one sorted list.\"\"\"\n    i = j = 0\n    out = []\n    while i < len(a) and j < len(b):\n        if a[i] <= b[j]:\n            out.append(a[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            out.append(b[j])\n            j += 1\n    out.extend(a[i:])\n    out.extend(b[j:])\n    return out\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(merge_sorted([1, 4, 9], [2, 3, 10, 11]))\n\n\nThe river ran high that spring, and the town council met every evening to argue about the levee. Some wanted to raise it by a metre; others said the money would be better spent moving the houses on the low road further up the hill. Nobody could agree on who should pay, and in the end the water decided for them: on the first warm night in April it came over the top near the old mill, quietly, and by morning the low road was a canal. The children loved it. Their parents did not.\n\ndef merge_sorted(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Merge two sorted lists into one sorted list.\"\"\"\n    i = j = 0\n    out = []\n    while i < len(a) and j < len(b):\n        if a[i] <= b[j]:\n            out.append(a[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            out.append(b[j])\n            j += 1\n    out.extend(a[i:])\n    out.extend(b[j:])\n    return out\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(merge_sorted([1, 4, 9], [2, 3, 10, 11]))\n\n\nThe river ran high that spring, and the town council met every evening to argue about the levee. Some wanted to raise it by a metre; others said the money would be better spent moving the houses on the low road further up the hill. Nobody could agree on who should pay, and in the end the water decided for them: on the first warm night in April it came over the top near the old mill, quietly, and by morning the low road was a canal. The children loved it. Their parents did not.\n\ndef merge_sorted(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Merge two sorted lists into one sorted list.\"\"\"\n    i = j = 0\n    out = []\n    while i < len(a) and j < len(b):\n        if a[i] <= b[j]:\n            out.append(a[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            out.append(b[j])\n            j += 1\n    out.extend(a[i:])\n    out.extend(b[j:])\n    return out\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(merge_sorted([1, 4, 9], [2, 3, 10, 11]))\n\n\nThe river ran high that spring, and the town council met every evening to argue about the levee. Some wanted to raise it by a metre; others said the money would be better spent moving the houses on the low road further up the hill. Nobody could agree on who should pay, and in the end the water decided for them: on the first warm night in April it came over the top near the old mill, quietly, and by morning the low road was a canal. The children loved it. Their parents did not.\n\ndef merge_sorted(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Merge two sorted lists into one sorted list.\"\"\"\n    i = j = 0\n    out = []\n    while i < len(a) and j < len(b):\n        if a[i] <= b[j]:\n            out.append(a[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            out.append(b[j])\n            j += 1\n    out.extend(a[i:])\n    out.extend(b[j:])\n    return out\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(merge_sorted([1, 4, 9], [2, 3, 10, 11]))\n",
